-          row_last_end(row_last_end) {}
+          row_last_end(row_last_end),
+          source_period_offset_tiles(source_period_offset_tiles) {}
+    // Appends the rectangles to dump for the tiles [range_start, range_end) of
+    // the current EDRAM addressing period, owned by render_target (whose base is
+    // rt_base), from a dump area with the given base, pitch and used row length
+    // in tiles. range_local_offset is 0 for the part of the dump area in the
+    // period of its base, and xenos::kEdramTileCount for the part after the
+    // dump area's EDRAM addressing wraps around.
+    //
+    // A render target owns the tiles from its base up to the base plus the
+    // EDRAM tile count, so the tiles of the range below its base are owned
+    // through EDRAM addressing wrapping (for instance, a depth buffer whose
+    // estimated extent reached past the end of the EDRAM into a color buffer at
+    // 0). The range is split at the base, and each part is dumped with the tile
+    // indices of the render target's addressing period
